# Surface plot of an array plot (new in XPPAUT 8.2)
# A cable of 40 excitable (FitzHugh-Nagumo) cells: a pulse starts at the
# left end and travels to the right.
#
# 1. Initialconds -> Go (keys I G).
# 2. Viewaxes -> Array (keys V A) and fill in:
#      Column 1: u1   NCols: 40   Row 1: 0   NRows: 150   RowSkip: 20
#      Zmin: -0.3   Zmax: 1   Autoplot: 0   ColSkip: 1          -> OK
#    Space runs across, time runs down: the pulse is a diagonal stripe.
# 3. Press Surface in the array window: the same data as a 3-D surface
#    (x = cell index, y = time, height = u).
#      drag              rotate
#      wheel or + / -    zoom
#      [ and ]           lower / raise the height
#      m                 mesh on/off        r   reset the view
#    GIF, PS and SVG save the picture (PS and SVG are vector and large).
#    Save session also puts it in figures/ while the Surface window is open.
# 4. Range in the array window (Still 0) makes an animated GIF of the
#    array plot, e.g. for d from 0.5 to 2 (the pulse is faster for larger d).
#
f(u,w)=u*(1-u)*(u-a)-w
param a=0.1, eps=0.01, g=2.5, d=1
# no-flux ends
du1/dt=f(u1,w1)+d*(u2-u1)
%[2..39]
du[j]/dt=f(u[j],w[j])+d*(u[j+1]-2*u[j]+u[j-1])
%
du40/dt=f(u40,w40)+d*(u39-u40)
dw[1..40]/dt=eps*(u[j]-g*w[j])
# start a pulse at the left end
u[1..4](0)=1
@ total=150, dt=0.05, nout=1, bounds=1000, maxstor=20000
@ xp=t, yp=u1, xlo=0, xhi=150, ylo=-0.4, yhi=1.1
done
